$NetBSD$

Preserve native GTK4 text editing and spellchecking in wxWidgets 3.2.
AI-assisted EmberBSD adaptation; wxWindows licence, like the upstream files.
GTK4 native text controllers own IME; GtkText batches native edits and
GtkTextBuffer user-action signals coalesce multiline changes. Use the common
libspelling TextBufferAdapter for multiline and mirrored singleline buffers.
Requires the shared GTK4 core patch's wxGTKKeyEvent/scrollbar boundary.
https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/migrating-3to4.html
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libspelling/-/tree/0.4.10

